# Environment variables — EVERY variant, including operator backups.
#
# This used to be `.env` / `.env.local` / `**/.env` only, which matched the live files and
# nothing else. Operators DO copy an env file aside before a cutover (`.env.bak-*`,
# `app/.env.bak-*`), and those copies were untracked but NOT ignored — in a PUBLIC repo,
# one careless `git add -A` away from committing a real secret.
#
# Keep the negations narrow: `*.example` files are TRACKED on purpose, and PR #8 exists
# because one of them once carried a real-looking 64-hex secret. See
# tests/test_env_files_cannot_be_committed.py, which fails if this block is narrowed again.
.env*
**/.env*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

# Logs
*.log

# Model files (large)
*.safetensors
*.bin
!requirements.txt

# Scraped property cache (regenerable via build_scraped_dataset.py)
app/data/scraped_property_listings.csv

# Playwright MCP artifacts
.playwright-mcp/
chroma_db_agent_memory/
app/chroma_db_agent_memory/

# Refactor implementation plan (local only)
REFACTOR_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md

# Packaging and persistent runtime cache
/build/
/dist/
/src/*.egg-info/
.runtime/
# ...and every sibling variant — the SAME hole as the env block above, different artifact.
# `.runtime/` with a trailing slash matches that one directory and nothing else, so the
# per-experiment trees an operator creates — `.runtime-fpon/`, `.runtime-hardening/`,
# `.runtime-fccontrol/` and the like — matched no rule.
#
# This is the class whose INSTANCE is already patched further down as
# `/evaluation/results/schema_compaction_ab_2026-07-22/` (a `git add -A` that swept an
# untracked results package in). Naming instances does not stop the next one; a guard does.
#
# Evidence packages under `.runtime*` are retained on disk and deliberately NEVER committed.
# Scoped to `.runtime*` on purpose: `evaluation/results/<package>/` trees such as
# `live_routed_98` and `phase2_ab_2026-07-19` ARE committed provenance and must stay tracked.
.runtime-*/
.runtime*.jsonl
*.sqlite3

# SearXNG live config: a runtime file the container mounts and chowns to its own
# uid. Tracking it causes git-vs-container ownership conflicts, so it's ignored;
# bootstrap from deploy/searxng-settings.yml.example (deploy/update.sh does this).
/searxng/settings.yml

# Local user credential store (password HASHES — never commit, even by mistake).
# Default lives under .runtime/ (already ignored) but pin the filename anywhere it lands.
users.json
**/users.json
users.json.tmp
**/users.json.tmp

# Untracked junk archive (moved-aside legacy files)
archive/

# Local model weights and generated artifacts
# (name-only patterns below also match files now living under archive/ and docs/archive/)
student_model_lora/
fine_tuning/student_model_lora/
*.safetensors
*.bin
UK_Rent_Agent_Technical_Report.*
quick_test_results.csv
diagnose_geocoding.py
**/.env

# Zoopla repair guide (local only)
ZOOPLA_REPAIR_GUIDE.md

# Next-gen architecture design doc (local only)
NEXT_GEN_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE.md

# Fine-tuning datasets (regenerable via fine_tuning/generate_data.py).
# The LoRA weights dir (fine_tuning/student_model_lora/) is already ignored above.
fine_tuning/train.jsonl
fine_tuning/val.jsonl
fine_tuning/test.jsonl
fine_tuning/dataset_raw.json

# Frozen one-off evaluation run artifacts (large events/raw-run streams + CSVs).
# Small summary/report files (*.json, *.md, .gitkeep) under evaluation/results/
# stay tracked as provenance; only the bulky run streams are ignored.
evaluation/results/**/*.jsonl
evaluation/results/**/*.csv

# Local schema-compaction measurement package; intentionally never committed.
# The evaluation/results/**/*.jsonl|csv rules deliberately keep *.json/*.md tracked as
# provenance, so this directory needs its own exact rule or `git add -A` sweeps it in.
/evaluation/results/schema_compaction_ab_2026-07-22/
